.TH SIGN-APPLES.SH "1" "June 2026" "sign-apples.sh 1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sign-apples.sh \- create detached macOS signatures and verify notarization
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sign-apples.sh
[\fI\,OPTIONS\/\fR] \fI\,--input-dir DIR --output-dir DIR \/\fR[\fI\,--\/\fR] \fI\,TARGET\/\fR...
.br
.B sign-apples.sh
[\fI\,OPTIONS\/\fR] \fI\,--input-dir DIR --output-dir DIR --project sv2-tp --release VERSION\/\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Create detached macOS signatures, apply them, and notarize each target.
TARGETs are paths relative to \fB\-\-input\-dir\fR: Mach\-O binaries or .app bundles.
The new \fB\-\-output\-dir\fR mirrors those paths and contains detached signatures
and, for app bundles, detached notarization tickets. Inputs are modified.
Project mode selects both Apple host triples and all supported binary names.
sv2\-tp signs sv2\-tp and test_sv2 for arm64\-apple\-darwin and x86_64\-apple\-darwin.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-env\-file\fR FILE
Configuration file (default: .env in working directory,
if present). Command\-line options override configuration
.TP
\fB\-\-certificate\fR FILE
PKCS#12 signing certificate and private key
.TP
\fB\-\-api\-key\fR FILE
App Store Connect API private key (AuthKey_<ID>.p8)
.TP
\fB\-\-key\-id\fR ID
App Store Connect API key ID
.TP
\fB\-\-issuer\fR UUID
App Store Connect issuer ID
.TP
\fB\-\-input\-dir\fR DIR
Root containing already extracted, unsigned targets
.TP
\fB\-\-output\-dir\fR DIR
New directory for signatures; must not already exist
.TP
\fB\-\-project\fR NAME
Select supported project targets (currently: sv2\-tp)
.TP
\fB\-\-release\fR VERSION
Release directory version; required with \fB\-\-project\fR
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show this help
.TP
\fB\-\-version\fR
Show version
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
SIGNAPPLE_CERTIFICATE
Alternative to \fB\-\-certificate\fR
.TP
SIGNAPPLE_API_KEY
Alternative to \fB\-\-api\-key\fR
.TP
SIGNAPPLE_KEY_ID
Alternative to \fB\-\-key\-id\fR
.TP
SIGNAPPLE_ISSUER
Alternative to \fB\-\-issuer\fR
.TP
SIGNAPPLE_PASSPHRASE
Signing key passphrase; prompt once if unset
.TP
SIGNAPPLE_NOTARY_PASSPHRASE
API key passphrase; defaults to signing passphrase
.IP
Set explicitly to empty for an unencrypted API key
.PP
These variables can also be set in .env (see .env.example). Precedence:
command\-line options, then environment, then file. File values are literal,
optionally quoted, without shell expansion. Credential paths in the file may
start with ~/; relative paths in the file resolve against its directory.
.PP
Requires Bash 3.2+, signapple, Python 3, and xcrun notarytool (macOS).
Every notarization must have a top\-level JSON status of Accepted.
On failure, no output directory is published; inputs may already be modified.
Use fresh extracted inputs when retrying. No downloads or Git operations run.
